_model: proposition
---
title: Proposition 25
---
order: 25
---
short_label: VII.25
---
statement: If two numbers are relatively prime, then the product of one of them with itself is relatively prime to the remaining one.
---
proof:

Let *A* and *B* be two numbers relatively prime, and let *A* multiplied by itself make *C.*

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="130" height="250" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="VII.25 diagram" src="propVII25.gif"/></noscript>
<script type="text/javascript">
    geomlib.init({
        canvasid: "canvas_0",
        background: "35,19,100",
        title: "VII.25",
        elements: [
            "A0;point;free;30,-1000;0;0",
            "A3;point;free;30,1000;0;0",
            "A1;point;lineSlider;A0,A3,30,30;0",
            "A2;point;lineSlider;A0,A3,30,110;0",
            "A;line;connect;A1,A2;black",
            "B0;point;free;65,-1000;0;0",
            "B3;point;free;65,1000;0;0",
            "B1;point;lineSlider;B0,B3,65,30;0",
            "B2;point;lineSlider;B0,B3,65,130;0",
            "B;line;connect;B1,B2;black",
            "U1;point;free;1000,0;0;0",
            "U2;point;free;1000,50;0;0",
            "C0;point;free;100,-1000;0;0",
            "C3;point;free;100,1000;0;0",
            "C1;point;lineSlider;C0,C3,100,30;0",
            "C2;point;proportion;U1,U2,A1,A2,A1,A2,C1,C3;0",
            "C;line;connect;C1,C2;black",
            "D1;point;lineSlider;A0,A3,30,140;0",
            "D2;point;cutoff;D1,A3,A1,A2;0",
            "D;line;connect;D1,D2;black"
        ],
    });
</script>
</figure>

I say that *B* and *C* are relatively prime.

Make *D* equal to *A.*

Since *A* and *B* are relatively prime, and *A* equals *D,* therefore *D* and *B* are also relatively prime. Therefore each of the two numbers *D* and *A* is relatively prime to *B.* Therefore the product of *D* and *A* is also relatively prime to *B.* [!just VII.24]

But the number which is the product of *D* and *A* is *C.* Therefore *C* and *B* are relatively prime.

Therefore, *if two numbers are relatively prime, then the product of one of them with itself is relatively prime to the remaining one.*

<div class="qed">Q.E.D.</div>
<br clear="all">
---
body:

This proposition says that if *a* is relatively prime to *b*, then *a*<sup>2</sup> is also relatively prime to *b*.

It's a special case of the previous proposition and hardly needs its own enunciation. It is used in @VII.27 and @IX.15.
